                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]Experienced on the Oculus Rift [/h1]\n\nYou can view my review & gameplay here: https://youtu.be/5VpKAE4hJ54\n\nThis is a 180 degree wave shooter with gesture-based magical attacks. You can choose fire or ice spells of varying effects. There are 3 levels, each with a few waves. Enemies are rats, skull flying bats, and some warlocks/witches. \n\nYou can spam the same spell over and over again. You could also try different spells. Doesn't seem to make any difference. Enemies will either run up right to you or they will run to a spot and do ranged attacks. Just spam your spell and you'll be fine. Whole thing can be completed in 15-20 minutes (maybe less). \n\nThere's a story. The story is a few texts. Mostly instructions on how to do the gesture-based spells. The gesture-based spells sometimes work. I would say some spells work very consistently with the gestures, while others maybe worked half the time. Just keep spamming it though.\n\nThe game was released in Early Access. The game feels like a demo. The devs, so far, have not kept any of their promises on the Early Access description. Basically, they lied and took my money and yours too if you happened to buy this game. Let this be another cautionary tale about Early Access games. \n\n[b]Rate 3/10. I would recommend NOT buying this game. It's not worth anything. It's a demo and a poor one at that.[/b]",
